  'several-reservoirs-critically-low-tshwane-2026-11-06',
  'Several Tshwane reservoirs remain critically low despite gains',
  'Utilities', '2026-11-06', 'EWN', 'https://www.ewn.co.za/2026/11/06/water-supply-stabilising-amid-critically-low-reservoirs-tshwane',
  'The City of Tshwane says water supply is improving in most areas, but reservoirs feeding Soshanguve, Klapperkop and the Magalies/Rosslyn system stayed critically low on Friday, 6 November.',
  'The City of Tshwane said on Friday that it was seeing gains in most parts of the network after weeks of reduced bulk supply from Rand Water and high household demand, even though several reservoirs were still dangerously depleted. Officials named the Klapperkop reservoir at 5%, the Soshanguve L Tower at 6% and the Magalies/Rosslyn system at 16%, well below the levels needed for stable pressure in the suburbs they feed.

Other zones showed smaller shortfalls: Mamelodi R3 and Eersterust were both at 20%, Clifton at 19%, Mabopane Main at 22%, Lotus Gardens at 29%, and Ga-Rankuwa East and Brakfontein at 33%. The Carina Street system averaged 42%, still below the roughly 55% the city says it needs to keep pumping safely to higher-lying suburbs, while the Garsfontein reservoir has recovered to 52%, with its own distribution network now relatively stable.

City spokesperson Lindela Mashego said technical teams were coordinating with the bulk supplier to steady output and nurse the weakest zones back up. He urged households everywhere in the metro to trim non-essential use, arguing that conserving water now speeds up how quickly reserves can be rebuilt for the hardest-hit suburbs, and the city again asked residents to fix leaking pipes and avoid hosing down cars or filling swimming pools while the network recovers.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.ewn.co.za/2026/11/06/water-supply-stabilising-amid-critically-low-reservoirs-tshwane", "https://www.yfm.co.za/2026/11/06/tshwanes-water-woes-unsafe-springs-and-critically-low-reservoirs/"]',
  'agent'
);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news (
  slug, title, category, published_date, source_name, source_url,
  summary, body, image_url, image_credit, image_source, verification_json, source
) VALUES (
  'tshwane-becomes-hung-metro-election-2026-11-08',
  'Tshwane becomes a hung metro after 4 November election',
  'Community', '2026-11-08', 'BusinessTech', 'https://businesstech.co.za/news/?p=883205',
  'No party won a majority on Tshwane council after the 4 November municipal election, final results show, making it South Africa''s third hung metro.',
  'Tshwane became South Africa''s third hung metro of the 2026 local government elections, after no party won outright control of the city''s 214-seat council in the vote on 4 November. The Democratic Alliance finished first with 34.37% of the proportional vote and 74 seats, short of a majority.

ActionSA was the biggest mover, growing from 8.6% in 2021 to 22.07% of the vote and 48 seats, while the ANC''s support fell from 34.6% to 20.22%, leaving it with 44 seats. The Freedom Front Plus held roughly steady on 7.63% and 17 seats, and the EFF dropped to 5.77% and 13 seats.

Tshwane has been governed by coalitions since 2016, and the metro had four different mayors between 2021 and 2024 as earlier coalition arrangements broke down. With no party holding a majority again, the parties that won seats on the new council must now negotiate a coalition before a mayor can be elected and the city''s new term of office can begin.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://businesstech.co.za/news/?p=883205", "https://www.businessday.co.za/politics/2026-11-05-live-updates-tshwane-becomes-third-hung-metro/", "https://www.ewn.co.za/2026/11/05/tshwane-mayoral-candidates-brace-for-possibility-of-another-coalition-government"]',
  'agent'
);
